thub.com/users/Steiger04/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Steiger04/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Steiger04/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Steiger04","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Steiger04/ioBroker.vis-2-widgets-collection/commits/ad888a89ad0b8f3fa4da0a233df4f4b7d7904110/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T15:14:36Z","email":"steiger04@posteo.de","name":"steiger04"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T15:14:36Z","email":"steiger04@posteo.de","name":"steiger04"},"message":"test(use-data): add styleData resolver characterization tests\n\nPin the observable contract of the resolver layer\n(params -> createPropertyResolvers -> getStyleData -> StyleData) so the\nplanned F1 refactor (extract the isSlider branches into a slider resolver;\nfold Gauge min/max into useData) cannot silently change resolution order.\n\nThe chain is fully pure — runtime seams live only in useData.tsx, which\npasses everything in as plain values — so the tests build a param literal\nwith hand-rolled getDataValue/formatSize closures, no vi.mock. Covers: full\ndefault + populated StyleData shapes, style-object fallbacks, the isSlider\nmarker tier positions (iconSize vs iconWidth differ subtly — pinned), the\nmarker resolvers, and the noIcon short-circuit.\n\nThis is Stufe 1 of F1 (the gate). Stufe 2 (the refactor) follows.","tree":{"sha":"478699ff99c02b6714dfea3ebf71d7d613ba536c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Steiger04/ioBroker.vis-2-widgets-collection/git/trees/478699ff99c02b6714dfea3ebf71d7d613ba536c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Steiger04/ioBroker.vis-2-widgets-collection/git/commits/ad888a89ad0b8f3fa4da0a233df4f4b7d7904110","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17086