ng src/components and keeping the @/pages public API.\n\nCo-authored-by: Junie <junie@jetbrains.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Junie <junie@jetbrains.com>","tree":{"sha":"d4f8052bf8f70e3dc712f3d142c6536e0ae2d472","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lcax-dev/lcax-apps/git/trees/d4f8052bf8f70e3dc712f3d142c6536e0ae2d472"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lcax-dev/lcax-apps/git/commits/16fb33b2594b761df4390c751fa6074c54b52b37","verification":{"payload":"tree d4f8052bf8f70e3dc712f3d142c6536e0ae2d472\nparent 02bbe1256cbf4c14e00a482f44b5d1b9bac963b9\nauthor Christian Kongsgaard <christian@kongsgaard.eu> 1788357392 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788357392 +0200\n\nAdd assembly editor, schema extensions, and dotenvx for config (#58)\n\n* Switch to `dotenvx` for encrypted environment variable management in development configuration.\n\n* Add `formatVersion` field to inputs schema, extend assemblies schema with `incomplete` boolean column, and create `organizationAssembly` GraphQL test suite.\n\n* Add AssemblyEditor components, live GWP calculations, save handling, and related tests; update routes and UI.\n\n* Upgrade LCAx to v3.6.0 and refactor AssemblyEditor components: add typename stripping utility, adjust layouts, and enhance error handling.\n\n* Colocate epd-search pages in per-page folders.\n\nMove each page, its tests, and page-private helpers into a named folder with a barrel, matching src/components and keeping the @/pages public API.\n\nCo-authored-by: Junie <junie@jetbrains.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Junie <junie@jetbrains.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmCsQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuscQAKwzRPvD1WgFXGnFNTiOaDnm\nwZBw8+ZOQnSwu7jPawe2fFHr0XqsD7fpL+mqmTCICTiZykgmlzI6vuPR8hKGZNNT\np8jxrkycP9B1bzhNuENLCIDW8472F/o7I3ZGNdqjB5IOhtTNb5MXE8GVvjwq5ZXa\nC8rXnG0Ej3YuoaOqJR6DQPg0y2hKum5g5Pcea57XVmnlYkooaV6NpeNEJma94dqo\nsJlpF9KxWMBEAcaKtQMDU2x3tsVloZxDdisnJsnvMlA2YkDs4WObuCLj0CLgbpq9\n1QSf0NAdF5FvnFj5K